Why use a controller?

Even though this function is small today, later you might want to:

Fetch leagues from MongoDB
Fetch teams
Load countries
Check permissions
Pass existing prediction data
Display flash messages

Instead of changing the route, you keep all that logic inside the controller.

For example:

exports.newPrediction = async (req, res, next) => {
    try {
        const leagues = await League.find().sort("name");

        res.render("predictions/new", {
            title: "Create Prediction",
            leagues
        });

    } catch (err) {
        next(err);
    }
};


